VLMF @VERSION@ for OpenVMS (vms-vlmf, @ARCH@) - EARLY TEST RELEASE
=================================================================

VLMF is a full-screen manager for the License Management Facility: it shows
every license in a license database and lets you register (add), modify,
remove, disable or enable and load licenses, with the LK201 keys and PF1 as
the GOLD key. It looks like VTREE (vms-vtree).

Starting it
-----------
    $ VLMF :== $VLMF:VLMF.EXE
    $ VLMF                       ! the system database, LMF$LICENSE
    $ VLMF SYS$LOGIN:TRY.LDB     ! or any other license database

It needs a VT100-compatible terminal of at least 24 x 80; with 132 columns the
list also shows the authorization and comment. On a terminal without colour,
DEFINE VLMF$DISPLAY MONO first. Help (or PF2) lists the keys; F10 or Ctrl/Z
leaves.

To try it without risk, work on a copy first:
    $ COPY SYS$SYSTEM:LMF$LICENSE.LDB SYS$LOGIN:TRY.LDB
    $ VLMF SYS$LOGIN:TRY.LDB

The keys
--------
  Up/Down, Prev/Next    move; GOLD Up/Down first/last
  Return, I             every field of the license
  A, Insert Here        register a PAK typed into a form
  GOLD A                register the PAKs in a file: a LICENSE ISSUE/PROCEDURE
                        file or a PAK listing, one form each
  E                     modify: units, termination date, comment, selection
                        weight, include or exclude nodes, reserve users
  D                     disable an active license, enable a disabled one
  R, Remove             remove the license
  L                     load it on this node
  F, Find               filter by product name (VMS*, C%%%%)
  S                     sort by product, producer, termination date, status
  H                     show the history records too
  GOLD W, Ctrl/W        read the database again; redraw

A diamond before a product means SHOW LICENSE lists it as loaded on this node;
a * after units or a date means it was modified from the PAK's value.

Safety
------
- VLMF changes licenses only with LICENSE commands, run in a subprocess. It
  never writes the database file itself.
- Every change shows the exact commands first and runs them only if you type Y.
- Before its first change in a session VLMF copies the database to VLMF$BACKUP
  (default SYS$LOGIN:VLMF_BACKUP.LDB); if the copy fails nothing is changed.
- Every command and its result is logged in VLMF$LOG (default SYS$LOGIN:VLMF.LOG).
- It never uses LICENSE ISSUE, COPY or MOVE, which disable or delete the source
  license.
- LMF never shows a PAK's checksum: a removed license can only be registered
  again from its PAK. Keep your PAKs.

Privileges are those of the LICENSE command: changing the system database
needs SYSPRV (or write access to the file), LOAD needs CMKRNL and SYSNAM.

Removing
--------
PRODUCT REMOVE VLMF. It deassigns VLMF$ROOT and VLMF.

Source, issues and the rest of the family: github.com/issinoho/vms-vlmf and
openvms.issinoho.com. MIT licence (LICENSE. in the installation directory).
